# Shell scripts must keep LF endings regardless of the committer's platform.
# Railway runs `bash start.sh` inside a Linux container; a CRLF shebang fails
# there with `/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter`, which reads as a missing binary
# rather than a line-ending problem and is a genuinely confusing hour to lose.
# Without this, correctness depends on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
